body:
@coderabbitai Both points verified; addressed in 407ca8d4.

Recovery: the background run now records the outcome. On failure it touches `github-app-advise.stamp.failed`, then removes the 6h stamp (in that order, so no window has neither). The next attempt waits only `AIDEVOPS_GITHUB_APP_ADVISE_RETRY_INTERVAL` (default 1800 s). Success clears the failed stamp. Sandboxed run with a stub `python3`: fail gives stamp=n failed=y; within retry, no run; retry success gives stamp=y failed=n; then held by the 6h stamp. shellcheck is clean and `test-pulse-graphql-budget-priority.sh` passes.

Early-return ticks: documented as exempt, not wired. A lock-busy tick means another full cycle holds the instance lock, and that cycle runs `_pulse_set_rest_core_budget_priority` and refreshes the advisory. Entry modes (self-check, dry-run, canary) and short-circuits (stop or pause) do not dispatch, so the advisory about dispatch throughput has nothing to refresh there. `.agents/reference/github-auth.md` now says "at the start of each full cycle" and lists those exempt ticks.

